      "name": "history-60-typed",
      "question": "Why?",
      "recognizedQuestion": "Why?",
      "answer": "Because a CUDA warp shares instruction issue: the GPU issues an instruction to the warp, and an active-lane mask determines which threads execute it. If threads disagree on a branch, each required path runs with only its participating lanes active, reducing useful parallelism. Modern GPUs support independent thread scheduling, but divergent paths still don’t execute as 32 fully independent instruction streams.",
